{"id":10158,"path":"/grammar-points/b1/verb-preposition/","parentId":341,"order":250,"section":"grammar-points","level":"b1","depth":3,"title":"Verb + preposition: Dependent prepositions","seo":{"title":"Verb + preposition: Dependent prepositions - Test-English","description":"Master verb + preposition combinations in English with this B1 Intermediate grammar lesson. Clear rules, charts and exercises. Practise now!","image":"/media/uploads/B1%E2%80%93verb_preposition.png"},"modified":"2026-03-03T09:04:18","kind":"lesson","parts":["<h3>Exercise 1</h3> <h5>Choose&nbsp;the correct prepositions to complete the sentences below.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"582\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 2</h3> <h5>Choose&nbsp;the correct prepositions for the following verbs.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"581\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 3</h3> <h5>Fill in each gap with the correct prepositions: <em>at, in, on, of, to, for, about, with</em>.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"583\"></div>"],"explanation":"<h2>Verbs &amp; prepositions: Dependant prepositions</h2> <p>Some verbs are usually followed by a preposition before the object of the verb. These prepositions are called dependant prepositions. Check the list of some of the most common of these verbs below.<br> <br> <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-29899\" src=\"/media/uploads/verb-dependant-preposition.png\" alt=\"Colorful grammar chart illustrating common verb and preposition combinations in English, categorized by 'to', 'for', 'at', 'in', 'on', 'of', 'with', and 'about'.&quot;\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" loading=\"lazy\"></p> <h6></h6> <h3>Example sentences</h3> <h4>To</h4> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li>He <strong><span>got married to</span></strong>&nbsp;his high school sweetheart last summer.</li> <li>She <strong><span>belongs to</span></strong> a book club.</li> <li>I always <strong><span>listen to</span></strong> music on my way to work.</li> <li>I <strong><span>look forward to</span></strong> the weekend.</li> <li>He <strong><span>said to</span></strong> me that he would be late.</li> <li>We <strong><span>talk to</span></strong> our parents every weekend.</li> <li>She <strong><span>writes to</span></strong> her pen pal in New Zealand every month.</li> </ul> <h4>For</h4> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li>She <strong><span>asked for</span></strong> a piece of advice.</li> <li>He <strong><span>applied for</span></strong> the job but didn’t get it.</li> <li>They <strong><span>are looking for</span></strong> the keys but can’t find them.</li> <li>I <strong><span>paid for</span></strong> the groceries.</li> <li>I<strong><span>‘m waiting for</span></strong> Sandra.</li> </ul> <h4>At</h4> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li>She <strong><span>arrived at</span></strong> the airport on time.</li> <li>He <strong><span>laughed at</span></strong> the comedian’s joke.</li> <li>He <strong><span>looked at</span></strong> the painting in awe.</li> <li>They <strong><span>shouted at</span></strong> the team in encouragement.</li> <li>She <strong><span>smiled at</span></strong> me when I entered the room.</li> </ul> <h4>In</h4> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li>She <strong><span>arrived in</span></strong> New York yesterday.</li> <li>He <strong><span>believes in</span></strong> being honest at all times.</li> <li>They <strong><span>invest in</span></strong> real estate as part of their business.</li> <li>They <strong><span>succeeded in</span></strong> passing all their exams.</li> </ul> <h4>On</h4> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li>He <strong><span>depends on</span></strong> public transport to get to work.</li> <li>She <strong><span>insists on</span></strong> having fresh coffee in the morning.</li> <li>They <strong><span>spend </span></strong><span><span>a lot of money</span></span><strong><span> on</span></strong> gadgets.</li> </ul> <h4>Of</h4> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li>She <strong><span>reminds </span></strong>me <strong><span>of</span></strong>&nbsp;her mother.</li> <li>He <strong><span>thinks of</span></strong> a new idea every day.</li> </ul> <h4>With</h4> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li>She <strong><span>argues with</span></strong> her brother a lot.</li> <li>He <strong><span>agrees with</span></strong> the proposed plan.</li> <li>They <strong><span>compare with</span></strong> each other too often.</li> <li>We <strong><span>spend time with</span></strong> our family during the holidays.</li> <li>He has decided to <strong><span>stay with</span></strong> his cousin for the summer.</li> </ul> <h4>About</h4> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li>She <strong><span>argues about</span></strong> politics frequently.</li> <li>He <strong><span>complains about</span></strong> the weather constantly.</li> <li>She <strong><span>dreams about</span></strong> becoming an astronaut.</li> <li>We often <strong><span>talk about</span></strong> our future plans.</li> <li>He <strong><span>thinks about</span></strong> changing his job frequently.</li> </ul>","quizzes":[{"id":582,"questions":[{"id":4959,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I waited <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> you for more than an hour. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["about","of","for","at"]}]},{"id":4960,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I'm looking forward <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> seeing you. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["at","about","to","for"]}]},{"id":4961,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>We arrived <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> the station too late. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["at","of","in","to"]}]},{"id":4962,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>We are thinking <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> going on a trip to Venice. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["in","at","to","of"]}]},{"id":4963,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Why are you shouting <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> me?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["to","at","in","of"]}]},{"id":4964,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>This book belongs <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> me.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["of","to","with","at"]}]},{"id":4965,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I never complained <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> my salary.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["of","in","on","about"]}]},{"id":4966,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I spent all my money <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> clothes. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["on","of","about","in"]}]},{"id":4958,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>He got married <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> his boss.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["with","of","to","on"]}]},{"id":4967,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>As soon as we arrived <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> Lisbon, we called our friends. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["at","in","on","to"]}]}]},{"id":581,"questions":[{"id":4948,"num":"1","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>She smiled _____ him, and he blushed. </div>","choices":[{"id":7630,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>to</span>"},{"id":7631,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>at</span>"},{"id":7632,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>on</span>"},{"id":7633,"letter":"D.","html":"<span>of</span>"}]},{"id":4949,"num":"2","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>He paid _____ the meal and she paid _____ the taxi. </div>","choices":[{"id":7634,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>to</span>"},{"id":7635,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>for</span>"},{"id":7636,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>-</span>"},{"id":7637,"letter":"D.","html":"<span>of</span>"}]},{"id":4950,"num":"3","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>He said _____ me that I was stupid. </div>","choices":[{"id":7638,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>at</span>"},{"id":7639,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>for</span>"},{"id":7640,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>with</span>"},{"id":7641,"letter":"D.","html":"<span>to</span>"}]},{"id":4951,"num":"4","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>He insisted _____ coming with us. </div>","choices":[{"id":7642,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>in</span>"},{"id":7643,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>at</span>"},{"id":7644,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>on</span>"},{"id":7645,"letter":"D.","html":"<span>about</